## What is pinned

The values live in one place each; this table only says where.

| What | Where |
|---|---|
| quantbox (engine): the commit a tag names, the tag beside it | `pyproject.toml` (`[tool.quantbox-line]`) |
| quantbox-datasets (the reader) | `pyproject.toml` |
| every transitive dependency, exactly | `pyproject.toml` `[tool.uv] constraint-dependencies`, `uv.lock` |
| the data: sha256 of each dataset's `prices.parquet` | `datasets.lock` |
| the timing (`execution.lag_bars`) | `config.yaml`, `arms.yaml` |

## Reproduce

```bash
export QUANTBOX_DATASETS_ROOT=/path/to/quantbox-datasets/datasets
uv sync
uv run quantbox run -c config.yaml            # the base run
uv run quantbox arms -c arms.yaml             # every arm, one summary
uv run pytest -m reproduction                 # re-run + diff against expected_metrics.json
```

The first time, capture the golden once the run is the one you mean:
`QUANTBOX_CAPTURE_GOLDEN=1 uv run pytest -m reproduction`, then commit
`expected_metrics.json`.

## Repin

Moving the engine is one command, which rewrites the quantbox SHA and tag, re-derives
every exact pin from the new ref and refreshes `uv.lock`:

```bash
quantbox line repin . --ref vX.Y.Z      # omit --ref for the latest tag
uv sync
uv run pytest -m reproduction           # red = the engine moved a number: a finding, not a nuisance
```

## Pre-registration

Written and **committed on its own BEFORE the first measured run**, one block per
hypothesis. The prose is for people; the fenced block is what the pre-run gate reads.
Every `<...>` below is a placeholder, and the gate refuses a run while any is left.

```yaml
prereg:
  id: <hypothesis-id>
  book: <a books[].name from system.yaml>
  primary_dataset: {{DATASET}}
  secondary_datasets: []          # robustness only; never decides the verdict
  runs: [artifacts]               # where THIS hypothesis's runs land
  criterion:
    pass_rule: <all legs | k of n arms>
    legs:
      - name: <leg>
        metric: <metric>
        threshold: <number>
        versus: baseline
  claim_test:                     # a significance test of the CLAIM, not only of the Sharpe
    method: paired-stationary-block-bootstrap
    draws: <number>
    mean_block: <number>
    seed: <number>
    min_probability: <number in (0, 1]>
  ex_largest_episode:
    relabel_to: inconclusive
  n_trials: <every arm and probe, including earlier configs for the same idea>
  liveness:                       # every key of system.yaml `liveness`, never looser
    <key>: <number>
```

## Findings

Results are written only as finding files: `findings/YYYY-MM-DD-<verdict>-<slug>.md`.
Scratch work lives in `scratch/` (ignored) and is deletable.
